omx-plugins (0.18.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * zynthian-bundle: libmvec.so.1 is on a bare trixie
  * meter-level: compare the level readings within omx-dsp's fast-maths bound
  * Remove the parameter-contract migration members
  * Test the param-contract table against omx-clap-core's layout
  * version 0.18.0: in place proven per plugin, quiet blocks skip the
    resolve, the dirty flag read acquire, omx-dsp 0.29.0
  * faces: the CLAP face reads its dirty flag acquire
  * faces: a read of the CLAP face's dirty flag must be acquire, a
    main-thread store release
  * faces: in place proven per plugin, quiet blocks skip the resolve
  * faces: regenerated, no SPDX header inside the core headers
  * omx-test-pool-voice: activates at the block sizes clap-validator asks, up
    to 16384 frames
  * gen: the vtable partial drops its own SPDX header, the core header
    carries one
  * recipe-selftest: the meter's bypass reading is the reference's; the face
    reads its own from the row (#132)
  * factory presets: plugin {id}, createdAt and modifiedAt, as plugin-hostd's
    schema has them
  * presets-check: every factory preset holds to plugin-hostd's preset schema
  * descriptor-view: a moved link is refused by the symbol tie, and read with
    an explicit control
  * ci: a pull request from a fork never runs on the cluster's runners
  * ci: the heavy jobs run where vars.OMX_RUNNER says (GitHub-hosted by
    default)
  * descriptors: state schema floor 3.7.0; the round trip counts the four new
    meanings
  * contract: floor omx-contract 3.7.1, regenerate the four descriptors it
    words
  * summaries read their numbers from the declaration (#267)
  * gen: a parameter's symbol is tied to the control its ref names (#267)
  * omx keyed gate and limiter publish their gain reduction; the de-esser's
    meter takes its range from the readout (#267)
  * recipes: core-vtable.h.tmpl carries its SPDX header (#132)
  * units: this tree defines no unit code; the docs follow omx-contract's
    sheet (omx-contract#145)
  * deb: the omx-contract command is a build dependency and the build runs
    make test whole (#268)
  * zynthian-bundle: read both shapes of lv2bench's output (#268)
  * gen: stop writing lv2:reportsLatency, which LV2 deprecates (#267)
  * ci: require the clap-validator event-ordering tests on every plugin
  * omx-test-sine-voice: render frame-major so NOTE_END reports stay in time
    order
  * faces: one CLAP face and one LV2 face in lib/, each plugin's file its
    descriptor (#132)
  * BUILDING: one CLAP face and one LV2 face in lib/, each plugin's file its
    descriptor (#132)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 05:30:47 +0000
